[b]PassivePhantoms[/b] changes how phantoms behave on [b]Paper[/b] and [b]Folia[/b]. They stay [b]passive[/b] until a player hits them or a player-shot projectile does. Optional [b]End[/b] and [b]Overworld[/b] spawn control with caps, [b]stuck[/b] handling, and [b]chorus-tree[/b] avoidance keep skies interesting without the usual chaos.

[b]Version[/b] [b]1.3.0-Dev2a[/b] (see [b]pom.xml[/b] when building from source). [b]Java[/b] 8+ per project build. [b]API[/b] 1.13+.

[b]Downloads and changelog:[/b] [url=https://modrinth.com/plugin/passivephantoms]Modrinth — PassivePhantoms[/url]

Prefer Modrinth for the newest builds. SpigotMC listings may lag.

[b]Support[/b] through GitHub issues, Discord [b]#plugin-help[/b], or Modrinth comments. Please do not use resource reviews as tech support.

[b]Features[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Passive by default[/b] Phantoms do not hunt players until provoked. Then they behave like angry vanilla phantoms.
[*][b]Projectile provocation[/b] Arrows, tridents, snowballs, and similar player projectiles can trigger aggression.
[*][b]Custom spawn control[/b] When enabled, use [b]allow_overworld_spawning[/b] and [b]allow_end_spawning[/b] (defaults: Overworld off, End on). End spawning uses your chance and interval from [b]config.yml[/b].
[*][b]Spawn cap[/b] Limit how many phantoms count near each player using [b]max_phantoms_per_chunk[/b] and [b]spawn_check_radius[/b].
[*][b]Movement help[/b] Stuck detection and optional [b]tree_avoidance[/b] nudge phantoms away from chorus clutter. Still experimental around dense chorus.
[*][b]Master switch[/b] [b]passive_phantoms_enabled[/b] restores full vanilla phantom behavior when false.
[*][b]Update checker[/b] Optional. Ops with [b]passivephantoms.notify[/b] can see in-game notices.
[/list]

[b]Commands[/b] [b]/passivephantoms[/b]

[list]
[*]No args shows version and usage.
[*][b]reload[/b] Reload [b]config.yml[/b]. Needs [b]passivephantoms.reload[/b].
[*][b]debug[/b] Toggle debug logging at runtime.
[*][b]status[/b] Plugin status and phantom-related info.
[*][b]list[/b] List currently aggressive phantoms.
[/list]

[b]Permissions[/b]

[list]
[*][b]passivephantoms.reload[/b] default op. Reload command.
[*][b]passivephantoms.notify[/b] default op. Update notifications on join when a new version exists.
[/list]

[b]Config outline[/b] [b]config.yml[/b]

[code]
config_version: 4

debug_logging: false
passive_phantoms_enabled: true
update_checker: true

phantom_settings:
  custom_spawn_control: true
  allow_overworld_spawning: false
  allow_end_spawning: true
  end_spawn_chance: 0.05
  end_spawn_interval_ticks: 200
  max_phantoms_per_chunk: 8
  spawn_check_radius: 64.0
  movement_improvements_enabled: true
  stuck_detection_ticks: 100
  stuck_threshold: 3
  stuck_distance_threshold: 1.0
  max_stuck_attempts: 5
  tree_avoidance_enabled: true
  tree_avoidance_radius: 3.0
[/code]

[b]Installation[/b]

[list]
[*]Download the JAR from [url=https://modrinth.com/plugin/passivephantoms]Modrinth[/url].
[*]Place it in the [b]plugins[/b] folder.
[*]Start or restart the server. Edit [b]config.yml[/b] then [b]/passivephantoms reload[/b] or restart.
[/list]

[b]Updating[/b]

[list]
[*]Back up [b]plugins/PassivePhantoms/[/b].
[*]Replace the JAR and restart or reload config.
[*]Compare your [b]config.yml[/b] with new defaults and merge new keys if you skip a full reset.
[/list]

[b]Support[/b]

GitHub issues, Discord [b]#plugin-help[/b], or Modrinth. Thanks for using PassivePhantoms.
